=== SURVEY ===
Web source of truth: web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/ExportStatusWidget.tsx (read end-to-end).
  Data: useExports() (ExportJob: fsmState) + useExportJobs() (admin ExportJob: status), merged &
        deduped by id (admin wins), sorted by STATUS_ORDER then createdAt desc.
  Compose: WidgetShell chrome; CompactView (1×) big-number activeCount + Running/Idle badge;
           StandardView list (max 15) with per-row filename/format/size/status-badge/relative-time,
           a MetricBar under processing rows, and a download link (wide, ready+filePath only).
  Helpers: fmtBytes (1-dp, "—" for ≤0), truncateFilename(basename, 28), normaliseStatus (lenient).
  i18n (namespace 'dashboard'): widget.exportStatus / exportActiveJobs / exportRunningBadge /
        exportIdleBadge / noExportJobs / exportDownload, plus per-row status labels.
Registry (web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/registry/system.ts): id 'export-status', category
  'system', default 2×4, min 1×2, max 4×40.
Native infra surveyed: SharedFacade/{StateHolderModel,LoadableState,AppContainer} (bind pattern);
  Components/{UI,DataDisplay,Feedback}; Design tokens; Localizable.xcstrings.
i18n catalog reality: keys are flattened under a `translation.` prefix, e.g.
  translation.widget.exportStatus='Export Status', .exportActiveJobs='Active Exports',
  .exportRunningBadge='Running', .exportIdleBadge='Idle', .noExportJobs='No export jobs',
  .exportDownload='Download'; per-row statuses map to existing
  translation.export.status.{queued,processing,ready,failed}; refresh/retry/error reuse existing
  translation.common.refresh / translation.common.retry / translation.queryError.title; freshness
  reuses widget.freshness.{offline,stale,updated}. (All verified present in the catalog.)

=== REASONING ===
Architecture (chosen): a fully native, Apple-idiomatic surface composed of
  (1) pure, framework-free reducer + domain model (ExportStatusReducer / ExportJobStatus /
      ExportStatusSourceJob / ExportStatusRow) — a verbatim port of the web merge/sort/count and
      fmtBytes/truncateFilename helpers, unit-testable in isolation;
  (2) a Shared-free feed mirror (ExportStatusFeed) of the facade LoadableState (ADR-013) + an
      aggregate snapshot (ExportStatusSnapshot) + a fully-derived ExportStatusViewState state
      machine (loading/empty/error/content with stale/offline/refreshing flags);
  (3) a binding seam (ExportStatusProvider) — the native analogue of the useExports/useExportJobs
      hooks; ExportStatusModel (@MainActor @Observable, the StateHolderModel pattern) owns the
      snapshot; ExportStatusFeedProvider lets the dashboard host map each shared
      StateHolderModel<LoadableState<…>> into a feed and wire onRefresh to ExportsStore/AdminStore.
      The view performs NO HTTP and references NO KMP symbol directly (ADR bind-via-holder).
  (4) the SwiftUI view rendering EVERY state with the real TS component library
      (TSSkeleton / TSEmptyState / TSBadge / TSMetricBar / TSAnimatedNumber / TSFreshnessIndicator
      / TSButton), compact/standard/wide layouts keyed off ExportStatusWidgetSize.
  (5) diagnostics seam (ExportStatusTelemetry) emitting P1/S11 `view.opened` with slug
      "ExportStatusWidget"; default OSLog sink emits the slug only (no PII, ADR-016).
Rejected: (a) constructing Shared.ExportsStore/AdminStore in the view — composition-root work that
  AppContainer.bootstrap explicitly defers and that is out of scope/allowed-files; (b) depending on
  the not-yet-ported WidgetShell primitive — would not compile; (c) using web status keys
  widget.exportQueued/… — absent from the native catalog (would render raw keys), so canonical
  translation.export.status.* keys are used instead; (d) a snapshot-testing library — none is
  vendored, so each rendered state is covered by deterministic ExportStatusViewState tests instead.
File layout: a single cohesive ExportStatusWidget.swift (closest to the `ExportStatusWidget.*`
  allowed-files intent). Only the cosmetic SwiftLint `file_length` threshold is relaxed via a scoped,
  justified `// swiftlint:disable file_length`; every other rule (incl. strict) is enforced.

